  "asserts_no_claim": true,
  "purpose": "Bind the active-word derivation and the RC-8 replication by hash before review.",
  "SUMMARY_LINES_READ_FROM_THE_ARTIFACTS": "Every figure below was taken from RESULTS.json, not from a producer's prose. Six Coordinator claims have been corrected by producers or reviewers this session.",
  "RANK_1_the_campaigns_first_derived_proposition": {
    "proposition_1": "For E^r = ARK_r.SR.SB.[ARK_i.MC.SR.SB].ARK_0, any bijective S-box, any key, any r in {1,2,3,4}, any nonempty active set A, any smask in 1..14: on EVERY trial W = 4 - |A|, and word j is preserved IFF j is not in A.",
    "frozen_before_the_arms_that_test_it": "The derivation was written and frozen at 18:11:55Z; the arms followed. 24/24 arms at r<=4 match exactly, ZERO violations. This is a confirmed prediction, not a fit.",
    "IT_REMOVES_A_RESULT_RATHER_THAN_CONFIRMING_ONE": "The r<=4 'saturation' six batches treated as a strong signal is a CERTAINTY. Three consequences, each of which subtracts from prior readings: (1) THE r<=4 STATISTIC IS BLIND TO THE SWAP MASK ENTIRELY -- smasks 1, 2, 4, 7 and 13 give byte-identical output, so it carries NO information about the yoyo swap at those rounds. (2) The BATCH-006 validator's amask=15 null control is the |A|=4 case of this same formula: the control and the signal are ONE FORMULA AT TWO POINTS, which is why the control behaved as it did. (3) The 'excess 2^30' ceiling is explained -- the rate is 1.0 because the event is certain, so that figure was never a magnitude.",
    "the_break_point_named_in_advance_and_then_measured": "At r=5 the swap point moves to z_3 and the argument needs Delta(y_2') = MC^-1(Delta(z_2')), but MC^-1 is linear in the difference VALUE while crossing SB^-1 delivers only the zero PATTERN. The producer's independent verifier checked that identity mechanistically: 60/60 at r<=4 and 0/60 at r=5. Measurement and argument fail at the same step, and the argument named it first.",
    "measurements": "r=4 amask=2 gives [16777216, 0, 16777216, 16777216] with whist a point mass at W=3; r=5 amask=2 gives 33 hits in 2^31 with [7,10,7,9] -- hits on ALL FOUR words, the active word taking the largest count. All four single-word amasks plus multi-word 3,5,6,9,12,7,15 match. A drawn S-box and a second key reproduce identical vectors.",
    "producer_flagged_gaps": "Its completion gate is NOT fully met: bit-for-bit reproduction of a recorded command was not run, because it would have been invocation 31 against a hard cap of 30. It flagged the run-count ambiguity rather than resolving it in its favour. It also names a SHARED-SPECIFICATION caveat: its verifier is independent in implementation but not in specification, so a misread convention would make both wrong together."
  },
  "RANK_2_the_replication": {
    "result": "ALL 27 DRAWS AGREE WITH BATCH-006 EXACTLY -- integer for integer on W_ge1_nontrivial, trivial_swaps_excluded, W_ge1_by_word, the full whist, and on key_hex, thread_seeds and sbox_first8. Zero disagreements, including the non-obvious cases (five draws with exactly 1 trivial swap excluded, one with 3).",
    "bound": "ALIVE = 25 of 27 under the STRICT frozen criterion. One-sided 95% Clopper-Pearson lower bound 0.7847000388575458 against BATCH-006's 0.784700038857546 -- agreement to double precision. ONLY THIS READING WAS REPORTED: no pooled bound, no not-DEAD reading, no second criterion computed.",
    "the_two_non_alive_draws": "B11 (X=6, tail 5.94e-4) and B25 (X=9, tail 1.13e-6). BOTH FAIL ON THE POISSON CONJUNCT -- exactly the conjunct the corrupted BATCH-005 quotation drops. The two draws separating 0.78 from 0.90 are the two the looser reading would have swallowed.",
    "instrument_independence": "rc8probe.c written for this task: byte-level SubBytes/ShiftRows/MixColumns rather than T-tables, the DIRECT inverse cipher rather than the equivalent-inverse form, the S-box from log/antilog tables over generator 0x03, and a word-oriented key expansion. Pinned to FIPS-197 C.1 both directions before measuring. Each drawn table verified byte-identical to BATCH-006's archived table, so a disagreement could not have been blamed on drawing a different object.",
    "what_it_does_and_does_not_buy": "IMPLEMENTATION AND SESSION INDEPENDENCE, NOT MODEL INDEPENDENCE -- both resolved to claude-opus-5. THE SAMPLE WAS NOT REDRAWN, so the 27 draws bound the preserving fraction exactly as much as before; what changed is that the instrument reading them is no longer single. It addresses EV-AES-9794e1's first unresolved confound and nothing else."
  },
